#: ../../../tools/iket.md:1
msgid "IKET Profiling"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/iket.md:3
msgid ""
"IKET is an experimental instrumentation tool for profiling TileLang CUDA "
"kernels. It adds named markers, warp-local ranges, and optional scalar "
"payloads to generated CUDA code. The external IKET profiler collects those "
"events and exports traces that can be inspected with Perfetto."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/iket.md:8
msgid "IKET is a CUDA tool, not part of the TileLang language namespace:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/iket.md:10
msgid ""
"import tilelang.language as T\n"
"from tilelang.tools.cuda import iket\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/iket.md:15
msgid ""
"The integration uses TileLang's regular `target=\"cuda\"` backend. It does "
"not depend on TileScale or the CuTe DSL frontend."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/iket.md:18
msgid "Requirements"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/iket.md:20
msgid "The target environment must provide:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/iket.md:22
msgid "TileLang with CUDA support"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/iket.md:23
msgid "A CUDA-capable GPU and driver"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/iket.md:24
msgid "PyTorch, when running the included examples"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/iket.md:25
msgid "The external IKET Python package and runtime"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/iket.md:27
msgid "Verify the active Python environment with:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/iket.md:29
msgid "python -c \"import tilelang, iket, torch\"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/iket.md:33
msgid ""
"The TileLang code-generation path supports both pre-Hopper and Hopper "
"targets. For SM90 and newer, generated instrumentation reads "
"`%cluster_ctarank`. For pre-Hopper targets, or when the target architecture "
"cannot be determined, it uses cluster rank `0` and does not emit the Hopper-"
"only register."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/iket.md:38
msgid "Quick Start"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/iket.md:40
msgid ""
"Construct and compile the instrumented kernel inside `iket.session(...)`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/iket.md:42
msgid ""
"import tilelang\n"
"import tilelang.language as T\n"
"from tilelang.tools.cuda import iket\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"def instrumented_add(n: int, threads: int = 128):\n"
"    @T.prim_func\n"
"    def main(\n"
"        A: T.Tensor((n,), T.float32),\n"
"        B: T.Tensor((n,), T.float32),\n"
"        C: T.Tensor((n,), T.float32),\n"
"    ):\n"
"        with T.Kernel(T.ceildiv(n, threads), threads=threads) as bx:\n"
"            with iket.range(\"block_total\"):\n"
"                for tx in T.Parallel(threads):\n"
"                    i = bx * threads + tx\n"
"                    if i < n:\n"
"                        iket.mark(\"before_store\")\n"
"                        C[i] = A[i] + B[i]\n"
"                        iket.mark(\"after_store\")\n"
"\n"
"    return main\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"with iket.session(output_dir=\"/tmp/tilelang_iket\"):\n"
"    program = instrumented_add(1024)\n"
"    kernel = tilelang.compile(\n"
"        program,\n"
"        out_idx=-1,\n"
"        target=\"cuda\",\n"
"        execution_backend=\"cython\",\n"
"    )\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/iket.md:77
msgid ""
"The session must be active when `tilelang.compile(...)` generates CUDA "
"source. Kernel construction inside the session is recommended because it "
"gives the session a fresh event registry, but it is not required. Event "
"metadata is embedded in TIR, so a `PrimFunc` constructed before entering the "
"session still retains the information needed during compilation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/iket.md:83
msgid ""
"Running a program directly compiles and executes the instrumented kernel. To "
"collect a trace, run the program through the external IKET profiler as "
"described below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/iket.md:87
msgid "Markers and Ranges"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/iket.md:89
msgid "Use `iket.mark(...)` for an instant event:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/iket.md:91
msgid "iket.mark(\"load_inputs\")\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/iket.md:95
msgid ""
"Use `iket.range(...)` as a Python context manager around a lexical region:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/iket.md:97
msgid ""
"with iket.range(\"compute\"):\n"
"    # TileLang statements\n"
"    ...\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/iket.md:103
msgid "The explicit range APIs are also available:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/iket.md:105
msgid ""
"iket.range_push(\"compute\")\n"
"# TileLang statements\n"
"iket.range_pop(\"compute\")\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/iket.md:111
msgid ""
"`iket.range_start(...)` and `iket.range_end(...)` are aliases for "
"`range_push(...)` and `range_pop(...)`. A range start can carry a payload, "
"but the range-end event cannot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/iket.md:115
msgid ""
"IKET records ranges at warp granularity. A block containing four warps can "
"therefore produce four trace ranges for one lexical `iket.range(...)` scope. "
"Names are limited to 32 UTF-8 bytes. Reusing the same marker or range name "
"with different payload dtypes in one frontend registry is rejected."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/iket.md:120
msgid "Runtime Payloads"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/iket.md:122
msgid ""
"Markers and range starts can capture one 32-bit scalar value. TileLang "
"currently supports these payload dtypes:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/iket.md:125
msgid "`int32`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/iket.md:126
msgid "`uint32`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/iket.md:127
msgid "`float32`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/iket.md:129
msgid "Use an explicit payload descriptor for TileLang expressions:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/iket.md:131
msgid ""
"iket.mark(\"store_index\", payload=iket.payload(i, dtype=\"int32\"))\n"
"iket.mark(\"scale\", payload=iket.payload(value, dtype=\"float32\"))\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/iket.md:136
msgid ""
"Simple Python scalars and expressions with a `dtype` attribute can be passed "
"directly, but an explicit dtype makes the trace schema unambiguous."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/iket.md:139
msgid "Runtime capture is opt-in:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/iket.md:141
msgid ""
"with iket.session(runtime_payloads=True):\n"
"    program = instrumented_add(1024)\n"
"    kernel = tilelang.compile(program, target=\"cuda\")\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/iket.md:147
msgid ""
"Without `runtime_payloads=True`, the payload schema remains encoded in the "
"TIR metadata token, but the emitted IKET metadata declares `NoPayload` and "
"the generated event writes no payload value. This keeps ordinary marker "
"records at four bytes. With runtime payloads enabled, the event emits "
"separate 32-bit timestamp and payload stores."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/iket.md:153
msgid ""
"Payloads are observed through IKET's warp-level dump mechanism. A payload "
"value usually represents the lane selected by that mechanism, not every "
"thread in the warp."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/iket.md:157
msgid "Compilation Sessions and Cache Behavior"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/iket.md:159
msgid "The full session signature is:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/iket.md:161
msgid ""
"with iket.session(\n"
"    reset_events=True,\n"
"    override=True,\n"
"    disable_on_exit=True,\n"
"    output_dir=None,\n"
"    runtime_payloads=None,\n"
"    disable_cache=True,\n"
"):\n"
"    ...\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/iket.md:173
msgid "The parameters control the following state:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/iket.md:175
msgid ""
"`reset_events` clears frontend event allocation for kernels constructed "
"afterward. Metadata already embedded in a `PrimFunc` is unaffected."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/iket.md:177
msgid ""
"`override` permits IKET to replace an existing "
"`tilelang_callback_cuda_postproc` callback while the outermost session is "
"active."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/iket.md:180
msgid ""
"`disable_on_exit` restores the previous callback by default. Leave this at "
"its default for scoped use."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/iket.md:182
msgid ""
"`output_dir` creates the directory, sets `TL_IKET_OUTPUT_DIR`, and "
"configures TileLang's IKET path helpers for the duration of the session."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/iket.md:184
msgid ""
"`runtime_payloads` temporarily selects whether payload values are emitted. "
"`None` preserves the previous setting."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/iket.md:186
msgid ""
"`disable_cache` bypasses TileLang's `KernelCache` by default and restores "
"its previous state when the session exits."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/iket.md:189
msgid ""
"Disabling the kernel cache is important even though event names and schemas "
"are part of the TIR cache identity. Callback activation and runtime payload "
"mode are host-side compilation state. Reusing a binary compiled without the "
"callback, or under a different payload mode, can therefore produce missing "
"or stale instrumentation. Set `disable_cache=False` only when the caller "
"controls those conditions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/iket.md:196
msgid ""
"The CUDA callback is reference-counted. Nested IKET sessions keep the outer "
"callback active, and leaving the outermost session restores the callback "
"that was registered before IKET. Output-directory, payload-mode, and cache "
"state are also restored after the session."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/iket.md:201
msgid "The lower-level lifecycle helpers are available for advanced use:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/iket.md:203
msgid ""
"iket.enable()\n"
"iket.is_enabled()\n"
"iket.disable()\n"
"\n"
"iket.enable_runtime_payloads()\n"
"iket.runtime_payloads_enabled()\n"
"iket.disable_runtime_payloads()\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/iket.md:213
msgid ""
"Prefer `iket.session(...)` so cleanup also occurs when compilation raises an "
"exception."
msgstr ""

