msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/iket.md:294
msgid "IKET ranges, markers, and runtime payload events in Perfetto."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/iket.md:297
msgid "The JSON export can be inspected programmatically:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/iket.md:299
msgid ""
"import json\n"
"from pathlib import Path\n"
"\n"
"trace_path = max(\n"
"    Path(\"/tmp/tilelang_iket_all_features_profile\").glob(\"*.trace."
"json\"),\n"
"    key=lambda path: path.stat().st_size,\n"
")\n"
"data = json.loads(trace_path.read_text())\n"
"launch = data[\"launches\"][0]\n"
"names = data[\"stringTable\"]\n"
"\n"
"store_indices = [\n"
"    marker[\"payloadVal\"]\n"
"    for marker in launch[\"markers\"]\n"
"    if names[marker[\"markerNameIdx\"]] == \"store_index\"\n"
"    and \"payloadVal\" in marker\n"
"]\n"
"print(store_indices[:8])\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/iket.md:320
msgid "Output Helpers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/iket.md:322
msgid "The CUDA tool includes small host-side helpers:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/iket.md:324
msgid ""
"iket.set_output_dir(\"/tmp/tilelang_iket\")\n"
"iket.output_dir()\n"
"iket.output_path(\"kernel.cu\")\n"
"iket.trace_files()\n"
"iket.profile_command([...], directory=\"/tmp/tilelang_iket\")\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/iket.md:332
msgid ""
"`trace_files(...)` returns `.trace.json` files ordered from largest to "
"smallest. The helpers manage paths and command construction only; they do "
"not collect a trace themselves."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/iket.md:336
msgid ""
"`iket.event_table()` returns the events registered while constructing recent "
"kernels. It is useful for inspection, but it is not the code-generation "
"source of truth. Call `iket.reset()` to reset frontend event allocation "
"explicitly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/iket.md:340
msgid "How Instrumentation Survives Compilation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/iket.md:342
msgid ""
"Each frontend event call carries a canonical metadata token in TIR. The "
"token contains the event name, kind, range identity, and payload schema. "
"This has two important consequences:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/iket.md:346
msgid ""
"A prebuilt `PrimFunc` retains its event metadata across session entry and "
"frontend registry resets."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/iket.md:348
msgid ""
"Structurally similar kernels with different event names have different IR "
"cache identities."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/iket.md:351
msgid ""
"While the session is active, `tilelang_callback_cuda_postproc` recovers "
"those tokens from generated CUDA, assigns module-wide event IDs, emits IKET "
"metadata arrays, and defines the NativeDump event macros. Event names are "
"not recovered from the process-local `event_table()` registry."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/iket.md:356
msgid ""
"No-payload events write one 32-bit timestamp/event record. Payload events "
"write the timestamp and payload with two separate 32-bit shared-memory "
"stores. The payload store is volatile so ptxas does not combine the pair "
"into `STS.64`, a record shape that the current external IKET patcher does "
"not accept."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/iket.md:361
msgid "Limitations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/iket.md:363
msgid "Only the TileLang CUDA backend is supported."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/iket.md:364
msgid "Runtime payloads are limited to `int32`, `uint32`, and `float32`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/iket.md:365
msgid "Event and range names are limited to 32 UTF-8 bytes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/iket.md:366
msgid ""
"Source-code location tables are not generated. Trace `locIdx` values are "
"IKET runtime location indices, not Python or TIR line numbers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/iket.md:368
msgid "IKET records events at warp granularity."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/iket.md:369
msgid ""
"The callback, payload mode, event registry, and kernel-cache switch are "
"process-global. Concurrent compilation workflows must coordinate access."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/iket.md:371
msgid ""
"The integration depends on private metadata and NativeDump conventions of "
"the external IKET runtime and should be treated as experimental."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/iket.md:374
msgid "Troubleshooting"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/iket.md:376
msgid "Payload schemas appear without `payloadVal`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/iket.md:378
msgid "Compile the kernel under a session with runtime payloads enabled:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/iket.md:380
msgid ""
"with iket.session(runtime_payloads=True):\n"
"    kernel = tilelang.compile(program, target=\"cuda\")\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/iket.md:385
msgid "Also verify that the marker has a supported payload descriptor."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/iket.md:387
msgid "The profiler fails while patching a payload kernel"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/iket.md:389
msgid ""
"Payload instrumentation requires two separate 32-bit stores. Inspect the "
"generated binary with:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/iket.md:392
msgid "nvdisasm kernel.cubin | grep -E \"STS|PMTRIG\"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/iket.md:396
msgid "The expected shape is:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/iket.md:398
msgid ""
"STS [addr], timestamp_with_event_id\n"
"STS [addr+0x4], payload_value\n"
"PMTRIG event_id\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/iket.md:404
msgid ""
"An `STS.64` for the timestamp/payload pair indicates that the "
"instrumentation sequence no longer matches IKET's NativeDump patching "
"convention."
msgstr ""
